## 2025-08-13 21:58:15 MIDI Timing Issue Root Cause Found
# PROBLEM IDENTIFIED: MIDI notes sent one step ahead of LED display
# ROOT CAUSE: Order of operations in process_tick() and advance_step() functions
# DETAILED ANALYSIS:
#   1. process_tick() calls advance_step() when tick_counter % ticks_per_step == 0
#   2. advance_step() calls process_step() BEFORE incrementing step counters
#   3. advance_step() then increments midi_step_count and other step counters  
#   4. process_tick() then calls play_midi() which uses the newly incremented midi_step_count
#   5. GridUpdate events are sent from advance_step() but processed later in main_loop()
# TIMING MISMATCH:
#   - MIDI events use step N+1 (after increment)
#   - LED updates show step N (current step being processed)
#   - Result: Audio plays one step ahead of visual feedback
# SOLUTION: Modify play_midi() to use step values BEFORE increment, or adjust when MIDI is played
# STATUS: Root cause diagnosed - ready to implement timing fix

