## 2025-08-16 14:36:52 MIDI Tempo Detection Algorithm Fix
# ISSUE: Major tempo discrepancy - clock generator outputs 121.0 BPM but sequencer detects 116-118 BPM
# ROOT CAUSE: Tempo detection algorithm calculated BPM from individual MIDI tick intervals
# PROBLEM: Individual tick timing susceptible to system jitter, USB latency, scheduling delays
# ALGORITHM FLAW: Single-tick calculation with no averaging or filtering
#
# FIX IMPLEMENTED: Beat-based tempo detection with rolling average
# NEW ALGORITHM:
#   1. Collect beat timestamps (every 24 MIDI clock ticks)
#   2. Maintain rolling window of last 8 beats (2 measures)
#   3. Calculate BPM from time span across multiple beats: BPM = (beat_count / time_span) * 60
#   4. Much more stable and accurate than tick-based calculation
#
# CHANGES MADE:
#   1. Updated ClockState struct to include beat_timestamps Vec<Instant> and last_beat_time
#   2. Modified handle_midi_input_message to use beat-based calculation instead of tick-based
#   3. Added rolling average over 8 beats for stable tempo detection
#   4. Reset beat timestamps in reset_clock() function
#
# EXPECTED RESULT: Sequencer should now detect 121.0 BPM matching clock generator output
# ACCURACY: Beat-based averaging eliminates individual tick jitter and system timing variations
# STATUS: Ready for compilation and testing - should resolve 3-5 BPM tempo discrepancy

